WEBVTT


00:00:18.935 --> 00:00:20.903
[KETTLE WHISTLING]


00:00:21.071 --> 00:00:22.800
MAN 1 [ON TV]:
Wrong, as usual.


00:00:22.972 --> 00:00:26.100
The United States' lack of action
in Eastern Europe...


00:00:26.276 --> 00:00:30.713
...proves that the Soviet Union 's aggression
at the Afghan border...


00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:34.043
...will not be opposed publicly
by the United States.


00:00:34.217 --> 00:00:35.479
[WHISTLING STOPS]


00:00:36.086 --> 00:00:41.422
Issue: The Soviet Union continued
its recent series of military exercises...


00:00:41.591 --> 00:00:44.822
...conducting a bomb test today
in the Bering Sea...


00:00:44.994 --> 00:00:48.930
...just 1500 miles
off the southern coast of Alaska.


00:00:49.099 --> 00:00:53.468
President Richard Nixon
issued this warning to the Soviets:


00:00:53.636 --> 00:00:57.128
MAN 2:
The United States does not start fights.


00:00:57.307 --> 00:01:00.970
Let it be clear we maintain our strength...


00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:03.942
...in order to maintain peace...


00:01:04.114 --> 00:01:07.845
...so any adversary
should ask themselves:


00:01:08.017 --> 00:01:11.077
"Do the consequences
of attacking America...


00:01:11.254 --> 00:01:13.882
...outweigh the potential benefits?"


00:01:14.057 --> 00:01:16.685
As a result of the Soviet activity...


00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.658
...the watchdog group
of nuclear scientists...


00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:25.233
...moved the Doomsday Clock
up to five minutes until midnight:


00:01:25.401 --> 00:01:29.701
destruction by nuclear war.


00:01:30.406 --> 00:01:32.101
Question:


00:01:32.375 --> 00:01:34.900
On a scale of zero to 10,
zero meaning impossibility...


00:01:35.078 --> 00:01:37.410
...10 meaning
complete metaphysical certitude...


00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:42.074
...what are the chances the Russians
will actually attack the United States?


00:01:42.252 --> 00:01:43.549
Pat Buchanan.


00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:45.051
Zero.


00:01:45.221 --> 00:01:47.849
The Soviets
would never risk going to war...


00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:51.858
...when we have a walking nuclear deterrent
on our side.


00:01:52.028 --> 00:01:54.496
You're referring, of course,
to Dr. Manhattan...


00:01:54.664 --> 00:01:58.760
...but does Dr. Manhattan's existence
guarantee world peace? Eleanor Clift.


00:01:58.935 --> 00:02:01.665
Well, it hasn 't
stopped the Soviet Union...


00:02:01.838 --> 00:02:06.502
...from stockpiling record amounts
of nuclear weapons.


00:02:06.676 --> 00:02:08.371
You don ' t think it' s just posturing?


00:02:08.545 --> 00:02:10.137
Maybe the reason
why the Soviets...


00:02:10.313 --> 00:02:12.838
...are doing these bomb tests...


00:02:13.016 --> 00:02:17.385
...is because they feel threatened
by Dr. Manhattan. Of course.


00:02:17.954 --> 00:02:21.082
Maybe the whole world feels like that.


00:02:21.257 --> 00:02:22.918
[MTV THEME "MAN ON THE MOON"
PLAYS ON TV]


00:02:23.092 --> 00:02:25.560
Soviet ships have violated
the territorial waters...


00:02:25.728 --> 00:02:28.288
[NAT KING COLE'S "UNFORGETTABLE"
PLAYS ON TV]


00:03:02.365 --> 00:03:04.629
Just a matter of time, I suppose.


00:03:24.254 --> 00:03:26.017
[GRUNTING]


00:04:29.986 --> 00:04:31.476
[YELLS]


00:04:32.555 --> 00:04:34.853
[CHUCKLES]


00:04:35.258 --> 00:04:38.921
It's a joke. It's all a joke.


00:04:39.562 --> 00:04:41.826
Mother, forgive me.


00:08:37.033 --> 00:08:40.059
[ARGUING INDISTINCTLY]


00:08:42.605 --> 00:08:45.574
SALLY:
I was a hero, goddamn it!


00:08:46.976 --> 00:08:51.140
MAN [ON TV]: an act clearly meant to send
a signal to the government in Saigon...


00:08:51.314 --> 00:08:55.648
...that violence and oppression
is not the way to peace.


00:09:32.989 --> 00:09:35.480
MAN 1:
Fuck you, pigs!


00:10:05.621 --> 00:10:08.749
MAN 2:
Good luck, Mr. Gorsky.


00:10:54.637 --> 00:10:57.697
MAN:
Get out of here, vigilantes!


00:10:57.873 --> 00:11:01.274
[CHATTERING]


00:11:05.414 --> 00:11:07.575
No!


00:11:31.607 --> 00:11:33.632
[SIRENS WAILING]


00:11:34.543 --> 00:11:40.675
GALLAGHER: Edward Blake. Sixty-seven
years old. Six-two, a solid 225.


00:11:41.183 --> 00:11:43.048
Guy was built like a linebacker.


00:11:43.219 --> 00:11:45.119
FINE:
Yeah, I saw the body.


00:11:45.287 --> 00:11:47.346
For a guy his age,
he was in terrific shape.


00:11:47.523 --> 00:11:50.185
GALLAGHER:
You mean apart from being dead?


00:11:51.427 --> 00:11:52.917
That's plate glass.


00:11:53.095 --> 00:11:55.996
You'd have to step on the gas
just to put a crack in it.


00:11:56.165 --> 00:11:58.224
Had to have been thrown.


00:11:58.401 --> 00:11:59.595
Check the bedroom?


00:11:59.769 --> 00:12:02.704
Yeah. Drawers opened, tossed through.


00:12:02.872 --> 00:12:05.932
Mattress flipped. Probably robbery.


00:12:06.108 --> 00:12:07.575
Or made to look like one.


00:12:07.743 --> 00:12:09.506
See this?


00:12:09.812 --> 00:12:13.043
- Shaking hands with the president.
FINE: Whoa.


00:12:13.215 --> 00:12:15.445
Think Blake was a spook?


00:12:15.618 --> 00:12:19.281
Government or black ops?


00:12:19.588 --> 00:12:21.488
GALLAGHER:
I think...


00:12:21.791 --> 00:12:25.090
...this is way bigger than both of us.


00:12:28.197 --> 00:12:33.499
RORSCHACH:
Rorschach's journal, October 12th, 1985.


00:12:33.669 --> 00:12:38.766
Dog carcass in alley this morning.
Tire tread on burst stomach.


00:12:39.041 --> 00:12:41.271
This city's afraid of me.


00:12:41.444 --> 00:12:45.380
I've seen its true face.
The streets are extended gutters...


00:12:46.048 --> 00:12:48.448
...and the gutters are full of blood.


00:12:48.617 --> 00:12:51.085
And when the drains finally scab over...


00:12:52.154 --> 00:12:54.384
...all the vermin will drown.


00:12:55.024 --> 00:12:57.424
The accumulated filth of all their sex
and murder...


00:12:57.593 --> 00:12:59.891
...will foam up around their waists...


00:13:00.062 --> 00:13:05.523
...and all the whores and politicians
will look up and shout, "Save us."


00:13:06.502 --> 00:13:10.131
And I'll whisper, "No."


00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:14.507
Now the whole world
stands on the brink...


00:13:14.677 --> 00:13:17.168
...staring down into bloody hell.


00:13:17.346 --> 00:13:20.873
All those liberals and intellectuals...


00:13:21.050 --> 00:13:23.041
...and smooth talkers...


00:13:23.219 --> 00:13:26.677
...and all of a sudden,
nobody can think of anything to say.


00:13:26.856 --> 00:13:30.019
Beneath me, this awful city.


00:13:30.192 --> 00:13:33.958
It screams like an abattoir
full of retarded children...


00:13:34.129 --> 00:13:38.759
...and the night reeks of fornication
and bad consciences.


00:14:49.872 --> 00:14:51.806
Huh.


00:14:59.348 --> 00:15:03.478
Tonight, a comedian died in New York.


00:15:03.652 --> 00:15:05.017
Somebody knows why.


00:15:05.955 --> 00:15:07.582
Somebody knows.


00:15:07.756 --> 00:15:09.280
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]


00:15:09.458 --> 00:15:11.653
[ELEVATOR DOOR OPENS]


00:15:12.861 --> 00:15:15.352
No, I definitely heard something.


00:15:18.701 --> 00:15:19.998
Watch the door.


00:15:40.055 --> 00:15:41.147
[GRUNTS]


00:15:45.294 --> 00:15:46.852
Shh.


00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:50.298
Must've been the wind. Next time you...


00:16:03.812 --> 00:16:10.047
MAN: It all started with the gangs.
You know, people tend to forget that.


00:16:10.719 --> 00:16:13.813
Pirate outfits, ghosts.


00:16:13.989 --> 00:16:16.583
They thought it was funny:
dress up and pull heists.


00:16:16.759 --> 00:16:18.124
[MAN CHUCKLES]


00:16:18.293 --> 00:16:20.989
As soon as we'd arrest them,
they'd be back on the street.


00:16:21.163 --> 00:16:24.997
Nobody could pick them out of a lineup
because of the damn masks.


00:16:25.167 --> 00:16:27.431
So a few of us cops, we get together...


00:16:27.603 --> 00:16:30.970
...and we figure, what the heck,
we'll mask up, too.


00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:33.836
We'll finish what the law couldn't.


00:16:34.643 --> 00:16:38.670
Pretty soon, the papers get wind of it.
They ran with it...


00:16:38.847 --> 00:16:42.510
...and oh, boy, we're a national pastime.


00:16:42.685 --> 00:16:46.177
It was me, Dollar Bill, Mothman...


00:16:46.355 --> 00:16:49.722
...Captain Metropolis, Hooded Justice...


00:16:49.892 --> 00:16:53.089
...Silk Spectre and the Comedian.


00:16:53.262 --> 00:16:56.789
Oh, don't get me started on him.


00:16:58.934 --> 00:17:02.995
I must be drunk already,
telling you this sob story again.


00:17:03.172 --> 00:17:05.037
I think you were trying to make a point.


00:17:05.941 --> 00:17:12.107
Well, my point is that we had it too easy.
It wasn't fair what happened to you guys...


00:17:12.281 --> 00:17:16.411
You guys who picked up where we left off.
- with Nixon forcing you out.


00:17:17.453 --> 00:17:21.913
Nixon, oh, that prick. To think I voted
for that prick five times.


00:17:22.091 --> 00:17:24.821
Hey, it was him or the commies, right?


00:17:27.629 --> 00:17:31.429
Oh, wow, it's almost midnight.
Gotta go.


00:17:32.968 --> 00:17:34.595
Truth?


00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:39.001
You were a better Nite Owl
than I ever was, Danny boy.


00:17:39.174 --> 00:17:42.905
- Hollis, we both know that's bullshit.
- Hey.


00:17:43.078 --> 00:17:44.340
Watch it with the language.


00:17:44.513 --> 00:17:47.141
This is the left hook
that floored Captain Axis, remember?


00:17:47.316 --> 00:17:48.681
- Yeah.
WOMAN [ON TV]: This just in:


00:17:48.851 --> 00:17:50.785
The masked vigilante
known as Rorschach...


00:17:50.953 --> 00:17:53.786
...has assaulted a police officer
in the early-morning hours.


00:17:54.656 --> 00:17:57.648
Rorschach is on the FBI's
Ten Most Wanted list...


00:17:57.826 --> 00:18:01.626
...for violation of the Keene Act,
which banned masked heroes six years ago.


00:18:01.797 --> 00:18:04.061
Rorschach reportedly incapacitated...


00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:07.000
Forced everyone out except him.


00:18:07.169 --> 00:18:08.693
Oh, he' II quit.


00:18:08.871 --> 00:18:10.202
When he' s dead.


00:18:10.839 --> 00:18:12.932
DAN: Next week?
HOLLIS: Well...


00:18:13.108 --> 00:18:17.704
...you know, you don't have to
keep humoring me like this.


00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:20.041
If you got a hot date or something...


00:18:20.215 --> 00:18:23.013
Hey, us retired guys
have to stick together, right?


00:18:24.787 --> 00:18:26.652
You ever miss it?


00:18:27.856 --> 00:18:29.949
No. You?


00:18:30.526 --> 00:18:32.323
Oh, heck, no.


00:18:33.629 --> 00:18:35.392
Be seeing you.


00:19:33.088 --> 00:19:35.955
[METAL SCRAPING]


00:19:49.171 --> 00:19:50.468
Hello, Daniel.


00:19:51.206 --> 00:19:52.298
Rorschach.


00:19:53.375 --> 00:19:57.675
Helped myself to some beans.
Hope you don't mind.


00:19:57.846 --> 00:20:00.280
No, no. Course not.


00:20:01.884 --> 00:20:04.444
You want me to heat those up for you?


00:20:04.620 --> 00:20:06.144
Fine like this.


00:20:07.723 --> 00:20:08.917
How have you been keeping?


00:20:13.295 --> 00:20:15.092
RORSCHACH:
Out of prison.


00:20:16.798 --> 00:20:19.028
Heard about you on the news.


00:20:19.635 --> 00:20:21.865
Say you attacked a cop.


00:20:22.037 --> 00:20:24.801
RORSCHACH: Minor wound.
Won't need hospitalization.


00:20:25.674 --> 00:20:26.834
Daniel...


00:20:27.009 --> 00:20:28.306
...Iook at this.


00:20:34.082 --> 00:20:36.710
DAN: Is this bean juice?
RORSCHACH: Human bean juice.


00:20:37.419 --> 00:20:41.913
Badge belonged to the Comedian.
Blood too. He's dead.


00:20:43.926 --> 00:20:45.393
Let's talk downstairs.


00:20:54.303 --> 00:20:56.066
DAN:
It could have been a burglary.


00:20:56.238 --> 00:20:58.934
Maybe the killer didn't know
who the Comedian was.


00:20:59.107 --> 00:21:03.840
RORSCHACH: An ordinary burglar?
Kill the Comedian? Ridiculous.


00:21:05.414 --> 00:21:08.850
I heard he'd been working
for the government since '77...


00:21:09.017 --> 00:21:12.180
...knocking over Marxist republics
in South America.


00:21:12.354 --> 00:21:15.289
Maybe it was a political killing
or something.


00:21:15.457 --> 00:21:16.719
Maybe.


00:21:16.892 --> 00:21:20.157
Maybe someone's picking off
costumed heroes.


00:21:20.329 --> 00:21:22.422
DAN:
You don't think that's a little paranoid?


00:21:22.597 --> 00:21:25.157
That what they say about me now?


00:21:25.400 --> 00:21:26.662
Paranoid?


00:21:26.835 --> 00:21:29.668
DAN: Look, Comedian made
a lot of enemies over the years...


00:21:29.838 --> 00:21:31.328
...even among his friends.


00:21:31.506 --> 00:21:33.667
RORSCHACH:
Speaking of friends, how's Hollis Mason?


00:21:34.543 --> 00:21:38.502
He wrote that book. Said some bad things
about the Comedian in it.


00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:42.741
I don't like what you're implying,
and I like being followed even less.


00:21:43.285 --> 00:21:47.745
Maybe I was keeping an eye on you,
in case someone's gunning for masks.


00:21:47.923 --> 00:21:52.587
- You were never that sentimental.
- Attack on one is attack on all of us.


00:21:53.028 --> 00:21:55.462
What do you suggest we do about it?


00:21:56.365 --> 00:21:57.525
Retribution.


00:21:58.934 --> 00:22:02.233
- Watchmen are over.
- Says Tricky Dick.


00:22:02.404 --> 00:22:04.167
Says me.


00:22:06.775 --> 00:22:08.402
Nobody knows who you are.


00:22:08.577 --> 00:22:11.546
You can give it up,
try and have a normal life.


00:22:11.713 --> 00:22:15.615
That what you have now?
A normal life?


00:22:16.618 --> 00:22:19.985
When you walk down the street
in a city dying of rabies...


00:22:20.155 --> 00:22:21.622
...past the human cockroaches...


00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:24.554
...talking about their heroin
and child pornography...


00:22:24.726 --> 00:22:26.250
...do you really feel normal?


00:22:27.396 --> 00:22:30.160
Least I'm not the one
still hiding behind a mask.


00:22:32.034 --> 00:22:33.296
No.


00:22:34.970 --> 00:22:37.097
You're hiding in plain sight.


00:22:38.473 --> 00:22:40.634
Be seeing you, Dan.


00:22:41.143 --> 00:22:43.611
A maintenance hatch
will let you out two blocks north.


00:22:43.779 --> 00:22:45.508
Yeah, I remember.


00:22:45.680 --> 00:22:49.741
Came here often,
when we were partners.


00:22:49.918 --> 00:22:51.818
DAN: Those were great times, huh,
Rorschach?


00:22:52.320 --> 00:22:55.551
- What happened?
- You quit.


00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:20.209
Rorschach 's journal.


00:23:20.382 --> 00:23:22.714
First visit of evening fruitless.


00:23:22.884 --> 00:23:24.977
Feel slightly depressed.


00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:27.420
Soon there will be war.


00:23:27.589 --> 00:23:31.150
Millions will perish
in sickness and misery.


00:23:31.326 --> 00:23:33.851
Why does one death matter
against so many?


00:23:34.596 --> 00:23:39.397
Because there is good and evil,
and evil must be punished.


00:23:39.568 --> 00:23:42.401
Even in the face of armageddon...


00:23:42.571 --> 00:23:45.369
...I will not compromise in this.


00:23:45.841 --> 00:23:49.436
But there are so many
deserving of retribution...


00:23:49.644 --> 00:23:51.908
...and so little time.


00:24:10.265 --> 00:24:11.630
[GASPS]


00:24:25.413 --> 00:24:27.074
MAN:
Captain.


00:24:27.249 --> 00:24:29.717
- Captain.
- Ridley.


00:24:29.885 --> 00:24:32.877
Ridley, have you seen
any other survivors?


00:24:33.054 --> 00:24:34.078
No, sir.


00:24:34.256 --> 00:24:38.716
Captain, my foot is caught
in some of the wreckage.


00:24:38.894 --> 00:24:42.261
- It's pulling me under.
- Hold on.


00:24:44.633 --> 00:24:46.464
Ridley.


00:24:47.335 --> 00:24:48.359
[SCREAMS]


00:24:57.546 --> 00:25:00.014
Ridley. Ridley.


00:25:00.649 --> 00:25:01.946
No.


00:25:02.117 --> 00:25:03.607
No.


00:25:03.985 --> 00:25:06.249
VOICES [CHANTING]:
More blood, more blood, more blood.


00:25:06.421 --> 00:25:08.912
MARINER:
Delirious from nearly drowning, I saw it.


00:25:10.492 --> 00:25:12.460
The Black Freighter.


00:25:12.794 --> 00:25:18.061
The hell-bound ship 's black sails
against the yellow Indies sky.


00:25:18.633 --> 00:25:24.572
I knew again the stench of powder
and men 's brains and war.


00:25:25.307 --> 00:25:29.471
VOICES [CHANTING]:
More blood, more blood, more blood.


00:25:35.350 --> 00:25:39.616
More blood, more blood, more blood.


00:25:45.794 --> 00:25:47.557
MARINER:
The waves about me were scarlet...


00:25:47.729 --> 00:25:50.721
...foaming, horribly warm
in the Freighter' s wake.


00:25:50.899 --> 00:25:54.062
In despair, I offered my weathered soul
to almighty God...


00:25:54.236 --> 00:25:57.728
...his mercy and his judgment.


00:25:59.274 --> 00:26:00.866
MAN:
Heh. What do you think, kid?


00:26:01.042 --> 00:26:04.136
We ought to nuke Russia
and let God sort it out.


00:26:04.312 --> 00:26:07.372
Or at the very least,
send Dr. Manhattan over for a visit.


00:26:07.549 --> 00:26:09.039
You know what I'm saying?


00:26:09.217 --> 00:26:12.118
I mean, I ain't trying to be an asshole
or anything, but they're the ones...


00:26:12.287 --> 00:26:14.778
...who are agitating us.
Now this is just my opinion.


00:26:14.956 --> 00:26:18.392
But I'm a news vendor, you know,
so I am informed.


00:26:19.160 --> 00:26:22.527
Yeah, I know. The New Frontiersman.
Well, it's not here yet.


00:26:22.697 --> 00:26:24.528
I'd appreciate if you didn't
stand around waiting...


00:26:24.699 --> 00:26:27.224
...because I don't know when
it's going to be here.


00:26:27.469 --> 00:26:29.403
I thought you said you was informed.


00:26:31.539 --> 00:26:34.508
- Are you gonna buy that?
- No.


00:26:36.411 --> 00:26:40.211
Oh, Jesus.
Just try again tomorrow, okay?


00:26:46.855 --> 00:26:48.015
[SIGHS]


00:26:50.659 --> 00:26:51.683
MAN:
Mr. Veidt...


00:26:51.860 --> 00:26:53.987
...to date,
you're one of only two Watchmen...


00:26:54.162 --> 00:26:56.596
...ever to reveal their true identity
to the world...


00:26:56.765 --> 00:26:58.562
...the first being Hollis Mason.


00:26:58.733 --> 00:27:01.725
And you've certainly profited greatly
by it...


00:27:01.903 --> 00:27:07.170
...turning your superhero alter ego,
Ozymandias, into a billion-dollar industry:


00:27:07.342 --> 00:27:10.402
Toys, lunchboxes, genetic engineering.


00:27:10.578 --> 00:27:12.637
I understand there's a movie
in the works.


00:27:12.814 --> 00:27:17.012
- I'm not hearing a question, Mr. Roth.
ROTH: I'm sorry. Do you think...


00:27:17.185 --> 00:27:19.745
The Watchmen resent me
for prostituting their struggle?


00:27:19.921 --> 00:27:22.651
It's a fair question.
Yes, it's crossed my mind...


00:27:22.824 --> 00:27:25.850
...some of my old colleagues
might see it that way...


00:27:26.027 --> 00:27:29.019
...just as you're clearly aware
that biased journalism...


00:27:29.197 --> 00:27:31.791
...sells more magazines.


00:27:32.300 --> 00:27:37.067
The merchandising arm of Veidt Industries
is funding our work with Dr. Manhattan.


00:27:37.238 --> 00:27:40.173
We recently expanded our research facility
in Antarctica...


00:27:40.342 --> 00:27:43.573
...in the hope of developing cheap,
renewable sources of energy...


00:27:43.745 --> 00:27:46.737
...that we might eliminate
the world's reliance on fossil fuels.


00:27:46.915 --> 00:27:49.349
Now, it doesn't take
a political scientist...


00:27:49.517 --> 00:27:52.918
...to see that our Cold War
with the Russians isn't ideological...


00:27:53.088 --> 00:27:56.580
...it's based upon fear.
Fear of not having enough.


00:27:56.958 --> 00:28:00.655
But if we make resources infinite...


00:28:00.829 --> 00:28:02.922
...ah...


00:28:03.098 --> 00:28:05.191
...we make war obsolete.


00:28:06.034 --> 00:28:09.868
I would hope the other Watchmen
understand that...


00:28:11.072 --> 00:28:12.733
...wherever they may be.


00:28:14.843 --> 00:28:16.208
Thanks for your time.


00:28:22.450 --> 00:28:25.112
- You look good, Adrian.
- Dan.


00:28:25.286 --> 00:28:27.516
It's been too long.


00:28:29.257 --> 00:28:33.318
ADRIAN: So Rorschach thinks
someone's hunting the Watchmen, huh?


00:28:33.995 --> 00:28:35.860
You think it's possible?


00:28:36.030 --> 00:28:38.760
Statistically, one murder
doesn't equal a trend.


00:28:39.901 --> 00:28:41.869
Rorschach's a sociopath, Dan.


00:28:42.504 --> 00:28:45.871
And so was the Comedian.
He was practically a Nazi.


00:28:46.708 --> 00:28:48.733
You know that better than anyone.


00:28:48.910 --> 00:28:51.105
I'm not here because I miss him.


00:28:51.279 --> 00:28:52.610
It's occurred to Rorschach...


00:28:52.781 --> 00:28:55.750
...that we're the only ones
who know each other's identities.


00:28:56.251 --> 00:28:58.344
Actually, the whole world knows yours.


00:28:59.120 --> 00:29:01.588
That's why I'm warning you first.


00:29:05.193 --> 00:29:07.184
Thank you, Dan...


00:29:08.797 --> 00:29:12.597
...but I fear there's something
much more real to worry about...


00:29:12.767 --> 00:29:15.361
...than Rorschach's mask killer.


00:29:16.871 --> 00:29:21.399
If the Russians do launch their nukes,
can Jon really stop them?


00:29:21.576 --> 00:29:25.205
The Soviets have 51,000
warheads stockpiled.


00:29:25.380 --> 00:29:28.577
Even if Jon stops 99 percent of them...


00:29:28.750 --> 00:29:32.948
...the 1 percent that get through
could still kill every living thing on Earth.


00:29:35.690 --> 00:29:38.056
Even Dr. Manhattan
can't be everywhere at once.


00:29:52.307 --> 00:29:57.939
Rorschach 's journal,
October 13th, 1985...


00:29:58.112 --> 00:30:00.444
...8:30 p.m.


00:30:01.149 --> 00:30:05.051
Meeting with Dreiberg
left bad taste in mouth.


00:30:05.253 --> 00:30:09.314
A flabby failure who sits
whimpering in his basement.


00:30:10.492 --> 00:30:13.461
Why are so few of us left active...


00:30:13.628 --> 00:30:18.497
...healthy and without
personality disorders?


00:30:18.666 --> 00:30:21.897
The first Nite Owl
runs an auto-repair shop.


00:30:22.070 --> 00:30:25.471
The first Silk Spectre
is a bloated, aging whore...


00:30:25.640 --> 00:30:28.507
...dying in a California rest resort.


00:30:28.676 --> 00:30:31.270
Dollar Bill got his cape stuck
in a revolving door...


00:30:31.446 --> 00:30:32.970
...where he got gunned down.


00:30:33.581 --> 00:30:36.015
Silhouette, murdered...


00:30:36.351 --> 00:30:39.286
...a victim of her own indecent lifestyle.


00:30:39.854 --> 00:30:42.846
Mothman 's in an asylum in Maine.


00:30:46.861 --> 00:30:51.059
Even Adrian Veidt, possible homosexual.


00:30:51.232 --> 00:30:53.723
Must investigate further.


00:30:53.902 --> 00:30:56.666
Only two names remain on my list.


00:30:57.205 --> 00:31:02.302
Both share private quarters
at Rockefeller Military Research Center.


00:31:02.477 --> 00:31:04.809
I shall go to them.


00:31:05.146 --> 00:31:10.516
I shall go tell the indestructible man
that someone plans to murder him.


00:31:11.319 --> 00:31:13.116
JON:
Good evening, Rorschach.


00:31:13.288 --> 00:31:16.780
RORSCHACH:
Dr. Manhattan, you know why I'm here.


00:31:16.958 --> 00:31:18.391
JON:
Yes...


00:31:19.661 --> 00:31:21.629
...but you're going to leave disappointed.


00:31:21.796 --> 00:31:25.527
Rorschach. You shouldn't be here.
You're a wanted man.


00:31:25.700 --> 00:31:27.895
RORSCHACH:
Nice to see you too, Silk Spectre.


00:31:28.069 --> 00:31:30.128
I have a real name I've been using.


00:31:30.305 --> 00:31:31.329
Try it.


00:31:31.506 --> 00:31:33.599
Whatever you say, Laurie.


00:31:33.775 --> 00:31:35.003
What are you doing here?


00:31:35.176 --> 00:31:37.508
JON:
The Comedian is dead.


00:31:37.679 --> 00:31:39.772
Rorschach wants me
to look into my future...


00:31:40.114 --> 00:31:42.582
...see if the killer is ever
publicly identified.


00:31:42.750 --> 00:31:45.844
Already warned Dreiberg.
Came to warn you too.


00:31:48.556 --> 00:31:50.922
Even if I wanted to help...


00:31:51.526 --> 00:31:55.428
...my future is blocked
by some kind of temporal interference.


00:31:55.830 --> 00:31:59.891
- I cannot see it clearly.
- Interference? Caused by what?


00:32:00.068 --> 00:32:03.469
In all likelihood, nuclear holocaust.


00:32:04.205 --> 00:32:08.301
If the United States and Soviet Union
engage in all-out war...


00:32:08.476 --> 00:32:12.469
...the resulting blast wave would produce
a sudden burst of tachyons...


00:32:12.647 --> 00:32:17.607
...particles which travel backward
through what you perceive as time...


00:32:18.252 --> 00:32:21.585
...therefore obscuring my vision
of the present.


00:32:22.390 --> 00:32:23.789
I must return to my work.


00:32:23.958 --> 00:32:25.084
RORSCHACH:
Wait a minute.


00:32:25.259 --> 00:32:27.750
What if that's why
someone wants us out of the way?


00:32:27.929 --> 00:32:30.159
So we can't do anything to stop it?


00:32:30.331 --> 00:32:32.162
Goodbye, Rorschach.


00:32:32.333 --> 00:32:34.597
RORSCHACH: Took a lot of effort
to get in here to see you.


00:32:34.769 --> 00:32:36.100
I'm not leaving...


00:32:37.372 --> 00:32:39.704
- till I've had my say.


00:32:47.215 --> 00:32:50.150
Seems like there's a lot of things
you don't tell me these days.


00:32:50.318 --> 00:32:53.014
I didn't wanna worry you prematurely.


00:32:53.488 --> 00:32:57.618
If Adrian and I can solve the energy crisis,
war may be averted.


00:32:57.792 --> 00:32:59.851
LAURIE:
But you always say time is simultaneous.


00:33:00.561 --> 00:33:03.428
If that's true,
then how can you change the future?


00:33:03.598 --> 00:33:08.592
If only you could perceive time as I do.


00:33:08.770 --> 00:33:10.032
Please let me show you.


00:33:16.010 --> 00:33:20.947
Magic. Dreams. That is what I had before.
I was a hero, goddamn it!


00:33:21.115 --> 00:33:24.175
It's not my fault you got old.
What do you have to complain about?


00:33:24.352 --> 00:33:26.786
I'm putting food on the table
for you and your child.


00:33:26.954 --> 00:33:29.718
Call your friend Eddie.
Maybe he can give you a better life.


00:33:29.891 --> 00:33:34.055
- It was a mistake. One time.
- Man tries to rape you...


00:33:34.362 --> 00:33:35.727
Stop!


00:33:36.497 --> 00:33:37.964
Your mind goes to dark places...


00:33:38.132 --> 00:33:40.464
...and you wonder
why I keep the worst from you.


00:33:44.405 --> 00:33:47.841
- Say hello to Dan for me.
- What?


00:33:49.610 --> 00:33:52.408
You wanna ask me
to go to dinner with you...


00:33:54.115 --> 00:33:56.276
...like we used to...


00:33:57.719 --> 00:33:58.845
...but you won't.


00:33:59.620 --> 00:34:01.884
You know I can't.


00:34:04.525 --> 00:34:06.789
So you'll call Dan...


00:34:07.228 --> 00:34:09.423
...which is only natural.


00:34:09.764 --> 00:34:12.358
You deserve the comfort of an old friend.


00:34:46.667 --> 00:34:48.191
LAURIE:
Dan Dreiberg's table.


00:35:09.357 --> 00:35:13.123
DAN: Did you know that
he and H.J. were...? I had no idea.


00:35:13.628 --> 00:35:16.688
You remember that crazy guy?
What'd he call himself?


00:35:16.864 --> 00:35:18.354
Captain Carnage.


00:35:18.533 --> 00:35:21.730
Used to pretend he was a supervillain
just so he could get beat up?


00:35:21.903 --> 00:35:24.303
Yeah, he tried that on me once.
I just walked away.


00:35:24.472 --> 00:35:27.498
He starts following me down the street
in broad daylight...


00:35:27.675 --> 00:35:30.473
...yelling, "Punish me! Punish me!"


00:35:30.711 --> 00:35:33.236
I'm just saying, "No, get lost."


00:35:34.382 --> 00:35:36.850
God, whatever happened to him?


00:35:37.018 --> 00:35:39.179
Oh. Um...
He pulled that on Rorschach...


00:35:39.353 --> 00:35:41.753
...and Rorschach
dropped him down an elevator shaft.


00:35:48.229 --> 00:35:50.629
Oh, my God. That's not even funny.


00:35:51.332 --> 00:35:53.823
- It's a little funny.
- Yep.


00:35:55.736 --> 00:35:57.704
WOMAN: I'm glad I ordered
the four-legged chicken.


00:35:57.872 --> 00:35:59.840
It's really good to see you again.


00:36:01.075 --> 00:36:02.599
It's great seeing you too.


00:36:03.411 --> 00:36:05.936
Why'd we do it, Dan? Dress up like that?


00:36:07.081 --> 00:36:10.414
- No one else would.
- Yeah, but do you remember my costume?


00:36:10.585 --> 00:36:13.679
All that tight latex?
I mean, it was awful.


00:36:13.855 --> 00:36:16.824
Uh... Yeah, yeah, awful.


00:36:16.991 --> 00:36:19.425
But didn't wanna disappoint Mother.


00:36:19.594 --> 00:36:23.587
Wanted her little girl to be just like her
and fight bad guys.


00:36:24.265 --> 00:36:27.860
I think the Keene Act was the best thing
that ever happened to us.


00:36:28.936 --> 00:36:31.302
Well, we'll live longer anyway.


00:36:34.609 --> 00:36:36.133
What?


00:36:37.111 --> 00:36:41.605
Jon thinks, unless he can do something
about it...


00:36:42.450 --> 00:36:44.475
...that there's gonna be nuclear war.


00:36:44.952 --> 00:36:46.442
Soon.


00:36:47.321 --> 00:36:50.654
But I don't know what to think.
I mean, it's all...


00:36:50.825 --> 00:36:53.885
...quantum mechanics
and parallel realities with him.


00:36:54.061 --> 00:36:56.825
I never even know
what universe he's actually seeing.


00:36:58.132 --> 00:37:01.260
He just keeps getting further away
from me.


00:37:01.969 --> 00:37:03.630
Everyone.


00:37:04.739 --> 00:37:07.401
I can't even tell
if he actually cares about me anymore...


00:37:07.575 --> 00:37:09.600
...or if he's just pretending.


00:37:10.311 --> 00:37:13.246
If he's pretending, it means he cares.


00:37:17.985 --> 00:37:19.976
Hold on, I'll get the door.


00:37:21.322 --> 00:37:23.119
Thanks, Dan.


00:37:23.491 --> 00:37:25.516
- Got it?
- Yeah.


00:37:30.932 --> 00:37:33.924
You always get
a government escort to dinner?


00:37:34.635 --> 00:37:38.696
They're making sure I don't do anything to
upset the country's most powerful weapon.


00:37:40.474 --> 00:37:41.702
I'm sorry.


00:37:41.876 --> 00:37:45.778
I invite you out to dinner to catch up
and have a few laughs...


00:37:46.147 --> 00:37:49.514
...but there don't seem to be many laughs
around these days.


00:37:49.684 --> 00:37:53.484
What do you expect?
The Comedian's dead.


00:39:33.287 --> 00:39:35.346
[VOMITING]


00:39:37.024 --> 00:39:40.585
Laurie? Is that you?


00:39:43.297 --> 00:39:46.266
Thought you'd be used
to traveling that way by now.


00:39:46.934 --> 00:39:50.927
Well, I'm not.
I hate it when Jon teleports me.


00:39:51.105 --> 00:39:53.972
Well, it beats flying coach.


00:39:54.341 --> 00:39:56.332
Margarita?


00:39:56.577 --> 00:39:58.738
Mother, it's 2:00 in the afternoon.


00:39:58.913 --> 00:40:00.881
[CHUCKLES]


00:40:01.449 --> 00:40:02.916
Mm.


00:40:03.584 --> 00:40:05.882
Remember that guy
that writes me letters?


00:40:06.253 --> 00:40:09.552
He sent me an item of memorabilia.
It's a Tijuana bible.


00:40:09.723 --> 00:40:13.887
This little eight-page porno comic
they did in the '30s and '40s.


00:40:14.061 --> 00:40:18.088
- He sent you this?
- Sure. They're very valuable, like antiques.


00:40:18.899 --> 00:40:20.594
Mother, this is gross.


00:40:20.768 --> 00:40:23.032
I think it's kind of flattering.


00:40:23.204 --> 00:40:25.468
Why do you always call me Mother
when you're mad?


00:40:26.841 --> 00:40:30.902
I know why you're here.
I can still read, you know.


00:40:31.679 --> 00:40:33.909
I saw it in the paper.


00:40:34.582 --> 00:40:37.483
Eddie Blake's funeral is today.


00:40:39.286 --> 00:40:42.278
Finally got his punchline, I guess.


00:40:42.756 --> 00:40:45.589
- Poor Eddie.
- Poor Eddie? After what he did to you?


00:40:46.293 --> 00:40:47.817
Oh, Laurie, you're still young.


00:40:48.596 --> 00:40:50.530
You don't know.


00:40:50.698 --> 00:40:52.461
Things change.


00:40:53.300 --> 00:40:56.064
What happened happened 40 years ago.


00:40:56.237 --> 00:40:59.502
I'm 67 years old.


00:40:59.673 --> 00:41:03.871
Every day, the future
looks a little bit darker.


00:41:04.712 --> 00:41:06.873
But the past...


00:41:07.381 --> 00:41:10.373
...even the grimy parts of it...


00:41:10.918 --> 00:41:13.546
...keep on getting brighter.


00:41:19.059 --> 00:41:21.892
I've got spots in my eyes.


00:41:23.631 --> 00:41:25.189
[SPEAKS INDISTINCTLY]


00:41:25.366 --> 00:41:28.028
Stop it, Eddie.


00:41:29.003 --> 00:41:32.370
- Thank you, Weegee.
- Thank you, Mr. Owl.


00:41:33.574 --> 00:41:36.771
Tomorrow, 3:00, my studio.


00:41:36.944 --> 00:41:40.107
- Little place on 21 st.
- Sounds good.


00:41:40.281 --> 00:41:44.877
SALLY: Wow, a real photo session.
Wonder how my hair will look?


00:41:47.188 --> 00:41:50.385
Oh, go ahead. I'll be there in five.


00:42:06.874 --> 00:42:07.898
Eddie.


00:42:08.976 --> 00:42:13.037
What the hell are you doing here?
You knew I was changing.


00:42:13.214 --> 00:42:14.806
Sure I did.


00:42:16.450 --> 00:42:18.042
Come on, baby.


00:42:18.485 --> 00:42:20.476
I know what you need.


00:42:20.654 --> 00:42:24.715
You gotta have some kind of reason
for dressing in an outfit like this.


00:42:24.892 --> 00:42:27.190
I said no, Eddie.


00:42:27.828 --> 00:42:32.731
- No spelled Y-E-S.
- No spelled N-O.


00:42:32.900 --> 00:42:36.336
- All right?
- Come on, sweetheart.


00:42:40.274 --> 00:42:41.866
Eddie...


00:42:45.079 --> 00:42:46.944
[GRUNTING]


00:42:50.718 --> 00:42:52.709
[EDDIE LAUGHS]


00:43:22.716 --> 00:43:25.446
You little bastard.


00:43:32.059 --> 00:43:33.083
This what you like?


00:43:33.260 --> 00:43:35.751
- This what makes you hot?
- What?


00:43:46.240 --> 00:43:49.437
Things are tough all over, cupcake.


00:43:49.610 --> 00:43:53.706
It rains on the just and the unjust alike.


00:43:53.881 --> 00:43:57.715
The Comedian was a little bit of both.


00:43:59.186 --> 00:44:02.553
And he always thought
he'd get the last laugh.


00:44:03.090 --> 00:44:06.150
MAN: Thou knowest, Lord,
the secrets of our hearts.


00:44:06.760 --> 00:44:10.093
Shut not thy merciful ears
to our prayers...


00:44:10.264 --> 00:44:14.860
...but spare us, Lord most holy,
O God most mighty...


00:44:15.035 --> 00:44:18.095
...O holy and merciful savior.


00:44:18.772 --> 00:44:21.502
Thou most worthy judge eternal.


00:44:21.675 --> 00:44:25.008
Suffer us not at our last hour
for any...


00:45:51.965 --> 00:45:54.399
EDDIE:
Fireworks. You gotta be kidding me.


00:45:54.568 --> 00:45:59.301
You know, you'd think this goddamn
country had had enough fireworks.


00:46:00.207 --> 00:46:02.801
You know, if we'd lost here in Vietnam...


00:46:02.976 --> 00:46:07.936
...I think it might have driven us crazy.
You know, as a country.


00:46:08.715 --> 00:46:12.412
But we didn't, thanks to you.


00:46:14.388 --> 00:46:16.322
You sound bitter.


00:46:16.490 --> 00:46:18.151
Me? Bitter?


00:46:18.325 --> 00:46:21.385
Fuck, no. I think it's hilarious.


00:46:23.230 --> 00:46:26.324
[JANIS JOPLIN'S "ME AND BOBBY McGEE"
PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]


00:46:27.734 --> 00:46:29.565
Oh, Jesus Christ.


00:46:29.736 --> 00:46:32.728
- Mr. Eddie?
- Just what I fucking needed.


00:46:32.906 --> 00:46:37.969
The war is over now.
We must talk about this baby.


00:46:38.745 --> 00:46:42.272
There's nothing to talk about.
See, I'm leaving.


00:46:42.449 --> 00:46:43.780
I'm gonna forget about you...


00:46:43.951 --> 00:46:46.784
...and your horrible, sweaty,
little piece-of-shit country.


00:46:47.354 --> 00:46:48.514
Get the fuck out of here.


00:46:50.257 --> 00:46:52.122
- No.
- Get the fuck out of here.


00:46:52.292 --> 00:46:53.657
You will remember.


00:46:55.429 --> 00:46:58.159
You will remember me and my country...


00:46:59.032 --> 00:47:00.659
...forever!


00:47:03.270 --> 00:47:05.135
My face!


00:47:07.341 --> 00:47:08.501
Blake. Don't.


00:47:09.309 --> 00:47:10.606
Blake!


00:47:17.484 --> 00:47:19.975
She was pregnant...


00:47:21.255 --> 00:47:22.984
...and you gunned her down.


00:47:23.156 --> 00:47:24.418
That's right...


00:47:24.591 --> 00:47:26.525
...and you know what? You watched me.


00:47:26.693 --> 00:47:29.685
You could have turned the gun to steam,
the bullets to mercury...


00:47:29.863 --> 00:47:33.458
...the bottle into goddamn snowflakes,
but you didn't, did you?


00:47:35.402 --> 00:47:38.235
You really don't give a damn
about human beings.


00:47:39.406 --> 00:47:42.239
You're drifting out of touch, doc.


00:47:43.810 --> 00:47:46.005
God help us all.


00:47:48.015 --> 00:47:49.312
Medic!


00:47:56.156 --> 00:47:59.319
MAN:
Most holy and merciful savior.


00:48:00.260 --> 00:48:05.163
He cometh up and is cut down,
like a flower.


00:48:05.332 --> 00:48:09.530
In the midst of life, we are in death.


00:48:09.703 --> 00:48:14.003
Of whom may we seek succor,
but of thee, O Lord?


00:48:18.412 --> 00:48:21.472
Welcome. We'll be starting shortly.


00:48:21.648 --> 00:48:23.741
We're waiting for one more.


00:48:34.528 --> 00:48:37.861
I told you, you wouldn't be
the only one dressed up.


00:48:39.499 --> 00:48:40.898
Welcome, doctor.


00:48:41.335 --> 00:48:42.962
Now we can start.


00:48:43.136 --> 00:48:46.970
Thank you for coming. Acquaint yourselves
with this map of high-crime areas.


00:48:48.342 --> 00:48:49.468
This is all bullshit.


00:48:50.277 --> 00:48:54.646
For a guy who calls himself the Comedian,
I can never tell when you're joking.


00:48:54.815 --> 00:48:58.216
Watchmen. That's the real joke.


00:48:58.385 --> 00:49:01.183
It didn't work 15 years ago,
and it ain't gonna work now...


00:49:01.355 --> 00:49:03.482
...because you wanna play
cowboys and Indians.


00:49:03.657 --> 00:49:06.023
Maybe we should agree
on no drinking at meetings.


00:49:06.193 --> 00:49:07.660
[LAUGHS]


00:49:07.828 --> 00:49:11.559
Rorschach and I have made headway
on the gang problem by working together.


00:49:11.732 --> 00:49:16.066
A group this size seems like
a publicity stunt. I'm not in it for the ink.


00:49:16.236 --> 00:49:18.033
ADRIAN:
We can do so much more.


00:49:18.205 --> 00:49:20.400
We can save this world...


00:49:20.574 --> 00:49:21.836
[EDDIE CHUCKLES]


00:49:22.009 --> 00:49:25.172
...with the right leadership.
- Yeah.


00:49:27.547 --> 00:49:29.310
And that'd be you, right, Ozzy?


00:49:29.483 --> 00:49:32.247
I mean, hell,
you're the smartest man on the planet.


00:49:32.419 --> 00:49:35.081
It doesn't take a genius
to see the world has problems.


00:49:35.455 --> 00:49:39.118
But it takes a room of morons to think
they're small enough for you to handle.


00:49:39.626 --> 00:49:40.786
You people.


00:49:40.961 --> 00:49:44.419
You hear Moloch's back in town,
get your panties all in a bunch.


00:49:44.598 --> 00:49:47.431
- You think catching him matters?
- Justice matters.


00:49:47.601 --> 00:49:48.829
[CHUCKLES]


00:49:49.002 --> 00:49:50.833
Justice.


00:49:51.438 --> 00:49:53.463
Justice is coming to all of us.


00:49:53.640 --> 00:49:55.107
No matter what the fuck we do.


00:49:55.842 --> 00:49:59.778
You know, mankind's been trying to kill
each other off since the beginning of time.


00:49:59.946 --> 00:50:04.781
Now we finally have the power
to finish the job.


00:50:05.018 --> 00:50:08.647
Ain't nothing gonna matter once
those nukes start flying. We'll all be dust.


00:50:11.792 --> 00:50:13.817
Then Ozymandias here...


00:50:14.828 --> 00:50:17.092
...will be the smartest man
on the cinder.


00:50:26.006 --> 00:50:28.065
MAN:
For as much as it hath pleased...


00:50:28.942 --> 00:50:33.208
...almighty God to take onto himself
the soul of our dear departed brother...


00:50:34.614 --> 00:50:38.675
...let us therefore commit his body
to the ground.


00:50:38.852 --> 00:50:42.310
Earth to earth, ashes to ashes...


00:50:49.396 --> 00:50:51.990
[CHATTERING]


00:50:52.165 --> 00:50:53.962
[GRUNTS]


00:51:06.079 --> 00:51:12.348
Watchmen! Police!
Police to protect the people!


00:51:16.890 --> 00:51:20.917
DAN: Attention, citizens.
We are trying to maintain order.


00:51:21.094 --> 00:51:25.531
You must clear the streets
until the police strike is over.


00:51:25.699 --> 00:51:28.862
If you could...
Please, there's no need for violence.


00:51:29.836 --> 00:51:33.932
We are trying to retain order on the streets
until the police strike is over.


00:51:34.107 --> 00:51:36.302
Crawl back in your holes
before you get hurt.


00:51:36.510 --> 00:51:38.637
- I got rubber bullets.
MAN 1: I want my rights!


00:51:38.812 --> 00:51:41.440
- You are not the law!
MAN 2: We want regular cops!


00:51:41.615 --> 00:51:42.877
No more vigilantes!


00:51:43.049 --> 00:51:46.610
My son's a police officer,
you fucking faggots!


00:51:48.221 --> 00:51:51.019
Goddamn it. All right.
That's how you wanna do it?


00:52:02.769 --> 00:52:04.430
There's no need for violence.


00:52:04.604 --> 00:52:07.732
Fuck you. Fuck you!


00:52:13.980 --> 00:52:15.709
Oh, this is getting heavy.


00:52:40.140 --> 00:52:43.541
Goddamn, I love working
on American soil, Dan.


00:52:43.710 --> 00:52:46.144
Ain't had this much fun
since Woodward and Bernstein.


00:52:46.313 --> 00:52:47.940
How long can we keep this up?


00:52:48.114 --> 00:52:51.709
Congress is pushing through some new bill
that's gonna outlaw masks.


00:52:51.885 --> 00:52:53.147
Our days are numbered.


00:52:53.320 --> 00:52:57.586
Until then, it's like you always say:
We're society's only protection.


00:52:57.757 --> 00:53:02.319
- From what?
- Are you kidding me? From themselves.


00:53:02.495 --> 00:53:04.690
- Son of a bitch.
DAN: No, Comedian, wait!


00:53:04.865 --> 00:53:06.059
[MAN GRUNTS]


00:53:06.233 --> 00:53:08.133
Get your stinking hands off me.


00:53:10.303 --> 00:53:12.771
What the hell happened to us?


00:53:17.077 --> 00:53:19.409
What happened to the American dream?


00:53:20.247 --> 00:53:23.080
What happened to the American dream?


00:53:23.250 --> 00:53:25.377
It came true!


00:53:25.552 --> 00:53:27.577
You're looking at it.


00:55:30.043 --> 00:55:31.510
Edgar William Jacobi.


00:55:31.678 --> 00:55:35.512
Also known as Edgar William Vaughn.
Also known as Moloch.


00:55:37.917 --> 00:55:39.384
[GROANING]


00:55:39.552 --> 00:55:41.816
What are you talking about?


00:55:42.756 --> 00:55:44.189
I'm a retired businessman...


00:55:44.357 --> 00:55:45.984
[GROANS]


00:55:46.493 --> 00:55:49.326
Lie again, Moloch, I break another finger.


00:55:49.496 --> 00:55:51.521
I did my time.


00:55:51.698 --> 00:55:54.496
I'm not Moloch anymore.


00:55:55.101 --> 00:55:59.538
- What do you want from me?
- Heard you attended Blake's funeral. Why?


00:55:59.706 --> 00:56:03.164
I just felt I should...


00:56:04.344 --> 00:56:07.245
...pay my respects to the Comedian.


00:56:09.716 --> 00:56:14.449
- How'd you know he was the Comedian?
- He broke in here. A week ago.


00:56:14.621 --> 00:56:16.953
He had his mask off.


00:56:17.424 --> 00:56:20.916
- He was drunk.
- Enemies. For decades.


00:56:21.094 --> 00:56:24.120
- Why should he visit you?
- I don't know.


00:56:24.297 --> 00:56:27.232
I woke up in my bedroom
and there he was.


00:56:27.400 --> 00:56:29.368
He was upset.


00:56:29.936 --> 00:56:31.460
He was crying.


00:56:31.971 --> 00:56:34.269
Crying? The Comedian?


00:56:34.441 --> 00:56:37.433
EDGAR:
He was babbling, not making any sense.


00:56:37.610 --> 00:56:40.602
I was pissing in my pants.


00:56:40.780 --> 00:56:43.078
I thought he was gonna kill me.


00:56:43.249 --> 00:56:45.513
RORSCHACH:
What did he say?


00:56:46.820 --> 00:56:48.481
It's a joke.


00:56:49.222 --> 00:56:51.782
It's all a fucking joke.


00:56:53.827 --> 00:56:56.227
You know, I thought I knew how it was.


00:56:56.396 --> 00:56:59.422
I thought I knew how the world was.


00:57:00.567 --> 00:57:03.229
I've done some bad things.


00:57:03.903 --> 00:57:07.498
I did bad things to women. I shot kids.


00:57:07.674 --> 00:57:09.938
In 'Nam, you know.


00:57:10.510 --> 00:57:11.943
But that was fucking war.


00:57:12.912 --> 00:57:14.243
This...


00:57:14.914 --> 00:57:17.576
I never done anything like this.


00:57:20.253 --> 00:57:23.188
God, here I am...


00:57:23.356 --> 00:57:25.449
...spilling my guts...


00:57:25.925 --> 00:57:27.415
...to one of my archenemies.


00:57:29.596 --> 00:57:31.928
But the truth is...


00:57:32.532 --> 00:57:37.128
...you're the closest thing to a friend I got.
What the fuck does that say?


00:57:41.040 --> 00:57:43.235
Shit.


00:57:44.777 --> 00:57:46.438
And your name...


00:57:46.613 --> 00:57:49.138
...your name was on the list...


00:57:49.349 --> 00:57:53.649
...along with Janey, you know,
whatever the fuck her name is.


00:57:53.820 --> 00:57:56.254
Manhattan's old girl.


00:58:00.460 --> 00:58:02.621
Mother, forgive me.


00:58:03.796 --> 00:58:05.457
EDGAR:
And then he left.


00:58:06.466 --> 00:58:11.062
I swear I don't know
what the hell he was talking about.


00:58:17.810 --> 00:58:19.778
Funny story.


00:58:20.246 --> 00:58:22.578
Sounds unbelievable.


00:58:23.349 --> 00:58:25.283
Probably true.


00:58:25.451 --> 00:58:28.147
So that's it?


00:58:28.321 --> 00:58:32.451
- I'm clean?
- You?


00:58:33.660 --> 00:58:34.991
Clean?


00:58:39.933 --> 00:58:41.025
Amygdalin.


00:58:41.201 --> 00:58:43.897
This phony medication
made from apricot pits.


00:58:44.070 --> 00:58:47.301
- It's illegal.
- Come on.


00:58:49.175 --> 00:58:51.507
Please don't confiscate that.


00:58:52.345 --> 00:58:55.143
I'm trying anything.


00:58:56.616 --> 00:58:58.106
I have cancer.


00:58:59.118 --> 00:59:00.449
What kind of cancer?


00:59:02.355 --> 00:59:05.381
You know the kind
you eventually get better from?


00:59:07.293 --> 00:59:09.284
That ain't the kind I got.


00:59:12.532 --> 00:59:16.491
Rorschach 's journal. October 16th.


00:59:16.669 --> 00:59:19.502
Want some of this?
Fifty bucks, I'll suck your cock.


00:59:19.706 --> 00:59:22.470
- Thought about Moloch 's story.
- Come on.


00:59:22.642 --> 00:59:24.576
Could all be lies.


00:59:24.744 --> 00:59:29.044
A revenge scheme
planned during his years behind bars.


00:59:29.215 --> 00:59:34.312
Fuck you. I make more in a week
than you make in a year, you fucking homo.


00:59:34.487 --> 00:59:36.079
But if it's true...


00:59:36.256 --> 00:59:38.520
...what could have possibly
scared the Comedian...


00:59:38.691 --> 00:59:40.556
...enough to cry in front of Moloch?


00:59:41.928 --> 00:59:42.952
What was it he saw?


00:59:44.731 --> 00:59:46.392
And that list he mentioned.


00:59:50.570 --> 00:59:53.971
Edward Blake. The Comedian.


00:59:54.140 --> 00:59:56.540
Born 1918.


00:59:56.709 --> 00:59:58.734
Buried in the rain.


00:59:58.911 --> 01:00:00.776
Murdered.


01:00:00.947 --> 01:00:04.974
Is that what happens to us?
No time for friends?


01:00:05.918 --> 01:00:09.081
Only our enemies leave roses.


01:00:09.389 --> 01:00:12.290
Violent lives ending violently.


01:00:14.260 --> 01:00:19.323
Blake understood.
Humans are savage in nature.


01:00:19.499 --> 01:00:22.195
No matter how much you try
to dress it up...


01:00:22.368 --> 01:00:24.495
...to disguise it...


01:00:24.671 --> 01:00:27.799
...Blake saw society's true face.


01:00:27.974 --> 01:00:32.604
Chose to be a parody of it. A joke.


01:00:32.779 --> 01:00:34.440
I heard joke once.


01:00:35.615 --> 01:00:39.415
Man goes to doctor, says he's depressed.


01:00:39.585 --> 01:00:43.453
Life seems harsh and cruel.


01:00:43.623 --> 01:00:47.491
Says he feels all alone
in threatening world.


01:00:47.660 --> 01:00:50.458
Doctor says treatment is simple.


01:00:50.863 --> 01:00:55.300
"The great clown Pagliacci is in town.
Go see him.


01:00:55.468 --> 01:00:57.459
That should pick you up."


01:00:57.970 --> 01:01:00.905
Man bursts into tears.


01:01:01.074 --> 01:01:05.408
"But doctor," he says. "I am Pagliacci."


01:01:07.413 --> 01:01:09.142
Good joke.


01:01:09.415 --> 01:01:11.315
Everybody laugh.


01:01:11.484 --> 01:01:13.645
Roll on snare drum.


01:01:14.153 --> 01:01:15.643
Curtains.


01:01:17.957 --> 01:01:19.390
HOLLIS: Hey, Bernie.
BERNIE: Yeah?


01:01:19.559 --> 01:01:21.652
HOLLIS: Can I get a Time magazine
from you there?


01:01:21.828 --> 01:01:23.955
BERNIE: Sure.
- How much you want for it now?


01:01:24.130 --> 01:01:25.392
For you, 2 bucks.


01:01:25.565 --> 01:01:28.159
Two bucks. Going up, huh?


01:01:28.334 --> 01:01:30.802
There you go. Thanks.


01:01:30.970 --> 01:01:32.597
Hey, I like your book.


01:01:33.072 --> 01:01:36.530
Hey, thanks, Bernie. I appreciate it.


01:02:14.113 --> 01:02:16.479
[CAWING]


01:02:21.387 --> 01:02:23.116
[GRUNTS AND COUGHS]


01:02:26.526 --> 01:02:31.896
MARINER: When I awoke,
I found myself upon a dismal beachhead...


01:02:32.231 --> 01:02:33.425
...with my men.


01:02:34.200 --> 01:02:36.930
Pieces of my men.


01:02:43.242 --> 01:02:46.177
It was all I could do for her...


01:02:46.345 --> 01:02:49.678
...though she had borne me
through seas of blood.


01:02:49.916 --> 01:02:54.216
Her damp embrace had prevented me
from drifting beyond reach.


01:02:54.387 --> 01:02:59.256
Yet this small comfort
was all I could offer.


01:03:09.101 --> 01:03:11.194
One of my crew lay ahead.


01:03:11.370 --> 01:03:14.362
Birds were eating
his thoughts and memories.


01:03:14.540 --> 01:03:15.802
Away. Yah!


01:03:15.975 --> 01:03:17.567
Yah! Get away.


01:03:20.246 --> 01:03:23.215
In hell, at least the gulls are contented.


01:03:25.151 --> 01:03:28.882
For my part,
I begged that they should take my eyes.


01:03:29.055 --> 01:03:32.183
Thus sparing me future horrors.


01:03:33.826 --> 01:03:35.521
[BREATHING HEAVILY]


01:03:35.828 --> 01:03:38.092
What time do you have to be
at your interview?


01:03:38.264 --> 01:03:39.891
JON:
Don't worry.


01:03:40.533 --> 01:03:43.024
We've got plenty of time.


01:03:43.202 --> 01:03:45.727
[BILLIE HOLIDAY'S "YOU' RE MY THRILL"
PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]


01:03:50.076 --> 01:03:52.271
Your finger's like licking a battery.


01:04:12.598 --> 01:04:15.362
God, Jon, stop. What are you doing?


01:04:15.535 --> 01:04:16.866
Please don't be upset.


01:04:17.036 --> 01:04:20.699
I always thought you liked this.


01:04:20.873 --> 01:04:22.272
LAURIE:
No.


01:04:23.776 --> 01:04:26.745
I don't... No.


01:04:27.580 --> 01:04:30.413
I don't want that.


01:04:30.683 --> 01:04:33.846
I don't know
what stimulates you anymore.


01:04:35.988 --> 01:04:39.617
Look, I know you were just trying...


01:04:41.427 --> 01:04:43.895
Are you working in here
while we're in bed together?


01:04:44.063 --> 01:04:47.499
My work with Adrian
is at a critical stage right now.


01:04:47.967 --> 01:04:51.130
- I didn't think it was necessary to...
- To what?


01:04:51.304 --> 01:04:54.831
To what? To tell me which one of you
is giving me a pity fuck?


01:05:03.983 --> 01:05:06.417
My attention was completely focused
on you.


01:05:07.019 --> 01:05:09.283
If you think there's a problem
with my attitude...


01:05:09.455 --> 01:05:11.685
...I am prepared to discuss it.


01:05:13.459 --> 01:05:17.190
You know how everything in this world
fits together except people.


01:05:17.363 --> 01:05:21.823
What am I to you?
Another puzzle to be solved?


01:05:22.001 --> 01:05:25.698
Have your men stand back.
I'm teleporting the reactor to Karnak now.


01:05:26.539 --> 01:05:29.474
You're my only remaining link
to the world.


01:05:37.249 --> 01:05:39.843
I don't want that responsibility anymore.


01:05:45.725 --> 01:05:47.852
He's all yours.


01:05:53.899 --> 01:05:56.265
ADRIAN:
Don't worry, Jon. She'll be back.


01:05:57.737 --> 01:05:59.932
No, she won't.


01:06:14.020 --> 01:06:18.582
MAN [ON TV]: He's been called
many things: Hero, weapon...


01:06:19.091 --> 01:06:21.559
...linchpin of our national security...


01:06:21.727 --> 01:06:26.255
...deterrent to nuclear war,
or a man to end worlds.


01:06:26.599 --> 01:06:29.159
Later tonight, Dr. Manhattan...


01:06:29.335 --> 01:06:34.295
...will answer my questions and yours
in an exclusive interview...


01:06:34.473 --> 01:06:39.342
...brought to you commercial-free
by Veidt Enterprises.


01:06:39.512 --> 01:06:40.911
[KNOCKING]


01:06:41.080 --> 01:06:43.571
[NAT KING COLE'S "UNFORGETTABLE"
PLAYS ON TV]


01:06:54.193 --> 01:06:55.455
Who is it?


01:06:55.628 --> 01:06:57.596
LAURIE:
It's Laurie.


01:07:08.474 --> 01:07:11.739
Sorry. I just had this new lock installed.


01:07:11.911 --> 01:07:14.379
I didn't know where else to go.


01:07:14.547 --> 01:07:17.710
Oh, it's okay. Come in.


01:07:25.157 --> 01:07:26.181
What's wrong?


01:07:27.493 --> 01:07:29.120
I left Jon.


01:07:29.829 --> 01:07:32.127
Oh, God.


01:07:32.598 --> 01:07:34.327
I'm so sorry.


01:07:34.500 --> 01:07:37.333
I don't know why I'm here. I just...


01:07:38.871 --> 01:07:41.339
I don't know anybody else.


01:07:42.174 --> 01:07:45.473
I don't know anybody
except for goddamn superheroes.


01:07:46.045 --> 01:07:47.706
That's okay.


01:07:47.880 --> 01:07:50.144
You probably just had an argument
or something.


01:07:50.316 --> 01:07:51.681
No, Dan.


01:07:52.218 --> 01:07:54.914
You don't know what it's been like
living with him.


01:07:55.087 --> 01:07:58.215
The way he looks at things now,
it's like he doesn't...


01:07:58.390 --> 01:08:00.858
...remember what they are.


01:08:01.193 --> 01:08:03.354
It's like this world, this real world...


01:08:03.529 --> 01:08:07.329
...to him,
it's like walking through mist.


01:08:07.500 --> 01:08:11.061
And people are just shadows.


01:08:12.638 --> 01:08:15.129
Shadows in a fog.


01:08:16.242 --> 01:08:19.609
God, how did everything
get so tangled up?


01:08:21.213 --> 01:08:23.204
I'm sorry, Dan.


01:08:23.949 --> 01:08:26.941
This is twice now
I've ruined your evening.


01:08:27.386 --> 01:08:30.378
Come on. I'm glad you came over.


01:08:30.556 --> 01:08:34.083
I was just gonna see Hollis
for our weekly beer session.


01:08:34.260 --> 01:08:36.251
You're more than welcome to join.


01:08:37.429 --> 01:08:40.728
In fact, I insist.


01:09:09.295 --> 01:09:12.093
[WOMAN GASPING]


01:09:13.232 --> 01:09:16.030
Terrific. Dr. Manhattan arrives
and no one thinks to tell me.


01:09:16.202 --> 01:09:18.102
WOMAN: He just...
- We don't have time for makeup.


01:09:18.270 --> 01:09:20.568
That blue is too light for television.


01:09:23.342 --> 01:09:25.333
Is that dark enough?


01:09:27.146 --> 01:09:30.047
PRODUCER:
Yeah, that's dark enough.


01:09:30.216 --> 01:09:33.879
BERNIE: The weight of the world's on him,
but does he quit? No.


01:09:34.053 --> 01:09:36.317
News vendors always cope. They're the...


01:09:36.488 --> 01:09:40.049
Oh, God, here comes
that homeless guy again.


01:09:40.492 --> 01:09:43.290
I told you, this month's issue
still hasn't arrived yet.


01:09:43.462 --> 01:09:47.125
Why do you care about that right-wing rag?
Those bastards don't give a damn.


01:09:47.299 --> 01:09:48.323
[HORN HONKS]


01:09:48.500 --> 01:09:50.798
Hold up. Here they come.


01:09:54.573 --> 01:09:57.098
- Seymour.
- Bernie, how's tricks?


01:09:57.276 --> 01:09:58.300
BERNIE:
Fine, fine.


01:09:58.477 --> 01:10:01.776
See this guy behind me?
Been bugging me all week.


01:10:04.683 --> 01:10:08.881
Maybe we should get a cab.
These are bad neighborhoods.


01:10:09.054 --> 01:10:12.683
Yeah, well, I'm in a bad mood.


01:10:25.271 --> 01:10:27.535
MAN 1: Girl.
MAN 2: What we got here?


01:10:27.706 --> 01:10:30.573
Here's a list of Pentagon-approved
no-go areas.


01:10:30.743 --> 01:10:33.541
Afghanistan will obviously come up,
but just play it cool...


01:10:33.712 --> 01:10:36.078
...and try not to get
into any tight corners.


01:10:36.248 --> 01:10:39.945
- a renowned nuclear physicist,
who, through a terrible accident...


01:10:40.119 --> 01:10:45.887
...was gifted with extraordinary powers,
capable of bending matter to his will.


01:10:46.058 --> 01:10:50.324
Today, the world knows him
as Dr. Manhattan.


01:10:50.496 --> 01:10:51.827
Welcome.


01:10:51.997 --> 01:10:54.557
[AUDIENCE APPLAUDING]


01:10:56.835 --> 01:10:58.063
JON:
Thank you.


01:10:58.237 --> 01:11:00.171
MAN 3:
That's right.


01:11:06.712 --> 01:11:09.510
Ms. Black, you have the first question.


01:11:09.682 --> 01:11:11.115
Dr. Manhattan, as you know...


01:11:11.283 --> 01:11:13.979
...the Doomsday Clock
is a symbolic clock face...


01:11:14.153 --> 01:11:17.714
...analogizing humankind's proximity
to extinction...


01:11:18.057 --> 01:11:21.049
...midnight representing the threat
of nuclear war.


01:11:21.226 --> 01:11:24.389
As of now, it stands at four minutes
to midnight.


01:11:25.030 --> 01:11:27.498
Would you agree that we're that close
to annihilation?

